.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER> double \fBcsmp::FluxEvaluator\fP< dim, USER >::FluxBalanceAndOutFlow (\fBNode\fP< dim > * const nptr) const"

.PP
stores FV flux balances computed from current facet fluxes and C0 concentrations; returns outflow from cell Like \fBFluxBalancesFromFacetFluxes()\fP, but returns the current outflow from the cell\&.

.PP
The latter is valid only for intact finite volumes (not at model boundary)\&. Else, a ficticious outflow is detected at inflow boundaries\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
this method relies on precomputed facet fluxes\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER> void \fBcsmp::FluxEvaluator\fP< dim, USER >::FluxBalancesAtBoundary (\fBNode\fP< dim > * const nd_ptr) const"

.PP
computes flux balances on boundary FVs, using precomputed facet fluxes; volumetric balances are set to zero From precomputed facet fluxes, \fBFluxBalancesAtBoundary()\fP computes:

.PP
.IP "0." 4
Nothing for FVs on the model boundary with Dirichlet concentration constraints\&.
.IP "1." 4
facet fluxes and flux balances of intact perimeter finite volumes that are not on the model boundary
.IP "2." 4
accumulation of facet flux-concentration products
.IP "3." 4
inflow if the the perimeter finite volume is truncated by the model boundary\&. This is determined from the AtBoundary() flag (flag!=NOT)\&.
.PP

.PP
In summary, this method computes flux balances and concentration-facet flux products where possible, at sliced boundaries inflow (+) concentration products are stored to C1\&. At such boundaries the influx is found from the flux balance and the FV cell's concentration\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
This method is only for perimeter nodes 
.RE
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER> void \fBcsmp::FluxEvaluator\fP< dim, USER >::FluxBalancesFromFacetFluxes (\fBNode\fP< dim > * const nptr) const"

.PP
computes balance of transport variable fluxes from precomputed facet fluxes and transport variable Computes and returns FV flux balance computed from pre-calculated thickness-weighted facet fluxes\&. The divergence of the volumetric flow is stored into the variable 'flux balance'\&. The volumetric flow * upstream concentration product is stored into 'new concentration'\&. Both, the flux balance and its product with concentration are stored on the node\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
this method relies on precomputed facet fluxes\&. 
.RE
.PP

